  "completedSection": "Aspect: VOC emissions from spray booths. Impact: Air pollution leading to potential health risks for workers and environmental degradation, including contribution to ground-level ozone formation. Significance Evaluation Criteria (ISO 14001 clause 6.1.2): 1) Scale of emissions (high volume of VOCs used daily); 2) Severity of impact (potential for respiratory issues and environmental harm); 3) Frequency (continuous operation); 4) Legal requirements (compliance with local air quality regulations); 5) Stakeholder concerns (worker health and community impact). Operational Controls: Use of low-VOC paints, proper ventilation systems, regular maintenance of spray booths, and training for workers on safe handling and application. Monitoring Requirements: Regular measurement of VOC concentrations in the air, periodic inspection of ventilation systems, and documentation of paint usage and waste disposal.",
